{
 "id": "joy-to-the-world",
 "version": 1,
 "reviewed": true,
 "title": "Joy to the World",
 "description": "Isaac Watts's Christmas hymn to the tune Antioch, in Lowell Mason's own four parts, for 2 to 4 singers: the first verse, bright and steady. The soprano and alto sing \"Let ev'ry heart prepare him room\" in thirds over the bass's held note, then the tenor and bass come in a bar behind with their own \"And heav'n and nature sing\", and everyone meets on the last \"sing\".",
 "language": "en",
 "difficulty": "beginner",
 "genre": [
  "hymn",
  "christmas"
 ],
 "style": "straight",
 "tempo": 120,
 "key": "D",
 "timeSignature": "4/4",
 "pickupBeats": 0,
 "credits": {
  "words": "Isaac Watts (1719)",
  "tune": "\"Antioch\", arranged by Lowell Mason (1839)",
  "arrangement": "Lowell Mason's four parts (1848), adapted by Stackapella"
 },
 "licence": {
  "words": "public domain: Watts died 1748",
  "tune": "public domain: Mason died 1872",
  "arrangement": "Mason's four parts (public domain: Mason died 1872, his co-editor George James Webb 1887): his tune, alto, tenor and bass, a semitone lower; the bass sings his small-note pedal under \"Let ev'ry heart\"; four notes changed so the duet has its thirds and the inner parts have no wide leaps; breaths written in for beginners",
  "recordings": "synthesized guides",
  "checked": null,
  "source": "Lowell Mason and George James Webb, The National Psalmist (Boston: Tappan, Whittemore, and Mason, 1848), p. 132, \"Antioch. C. M.\", in four parts in E-flat, printed in 2/2 and written here in crotchets (4/4), a semitone lower in D; verse 1 as printed under the music; Boston Public Library copy, read from the scan at archive.org/details/nationalpsalmist00maso/page/n135. Mason's first printing of the tune, The Modern Psalmist (Boston: Wilkins and Carter, 1839), p. 144, in D (archive.org/details/modernpsalmistco00maso/page/n149), was compared: the 1848 page, \"republished from Carmina Sacra in an improved form\", is the one with the tenor and bass entries on \"And heav'n and nature sing\""
 },
